  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "Approved immutable Verify commands execute through a fixed non-login POSIX shell without operator startup configuration, preserving bounded execution and real revision-bound evidence.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution_result.mjs",
        "lib/gh.mjs",
        "lib/prd.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/config.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "The sole coordinator Verify launcher uses /bin/sh -c with the approved command text; absent and invalid SHELL cannot select another executable.",
        "The existing execFileAsync helper retains UTF-8 output, actual exit/error handling, the owned cwd, 120-second timeout and 256 KiB bound.",
        "Native quoted assignments, literal metacharacters, pipelines and PWD output use the exact approved commands. Injected ENV/BASH_ENV startup scripts are not executed.",
        "Failure evidence retains exit 23 and a blocked verification-failed checkpoint; three later reconciliations cannot replay commands or publish. Successful published replay cannot repeat verification.",
        "Existing focused regressions retain redaction, dirty/staged/untracked checkout rejection, head freshness, cancellation and lost publication-reply behavior.",
        "Canonical tick settlement and corrective resume remain responsible for previously blocked verification; old evidence is not cleared to retry.",
        "Configuration uses a separate zsh login lookup to discover executable PATH; it does not execute approved Verify commands and is unchanged.",
        "No schema, task lifecycle, harness adapter, model/provider default, execution consent, limited preparation authority or sandbox permission changed."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "approved verification uses a fixed non-login POSIX shell with missing or invalid SHELL",
        "non-login POSIX verification failures keep bounded evidence and do not replay"
      ]
    }
  ],
